pped sandstone mountain near Maseru in Lesotho, which Moshoeshoe I made his stronghold and capital in 1824.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/thabo-mbeki"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thabo-mbeki.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Thabo Mbeki</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Thabo Mbeki is a South African politician who was president of South Africa from 1999 to 2008, succeeding Nelson Mandela.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/thado-minbya"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thado-minbya.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Thado Minbya</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Thado Minbya was the founder of the Ava kingdom in Upper Burma.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/thado-minsaw-of-prome"><span class="enc-name">Thado Minsaw of Prome</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Thado Minsaw was a son of King Narapati of Ava and governor of Prome who rebelled in 1482 during a succession crisis and made Prome an independent kingdom.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/thaenae"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thaenae.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Thaenae</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Thaenae was an ancient port town on the eastern coast of Tunisia, just south of modern Sfax, at the site now called Thyna.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/thagaste"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thagaste.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Thagaste</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Thagaste was a Roman town in Numidia, on the site of modern Souk Ahras in north-eastern Alg