km east of Karachi.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/thaya"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thaya.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Thaya</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Thaya (Czech Dyje) is a river in Austria and the Czech Republic, about 235 kilometres long.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/theagenes-of-megara"><span class="enc-name">Theagenes of Megara</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Theagenes was tyrant of Megara in Greece in the second half of the seventh century BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/theatre"><span class="enc-name">Theatre</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Theatre is the performance of drama before an audience, and also the buildings designed for it.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/thebaid"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thebaid.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Thebaid</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Thebaid was the southern region of ancient Egypt around Thebes, stretching from about Abydos to the First Cataract at Aswan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/thebe-of-pherae"><span class="enc-name">Thebe of Pherae</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Thebe of Pherae was a daughter of Jason of Pherae and the wife of Alexander, tyrant of Pherae in Thessaly.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/thebes"><span class="enc-name">Thebes</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Thebes was an ancient city in Upper Egypt on the Nile, the site of present-day Luxor.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/thebes-greece"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thebes-greece.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Thebes, Greece</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Thebes was the leading city of Boeotia in central Greece and the dominant member of the Boeotian League.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/thefarie-velianas"><span class="enc-name">Thefarie Velianas</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Thefarie Velianas was a ruler of the Etruscan city of Caere around 500 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/thein-sein"><span class="enc-name">Thein Sein</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Thein Sein is a Myanmar general and politician who was prime minister from 2007 and president from 2011 to 2016.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aethelbald-of-mercia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelbald-of-mercia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Æthelbald of Mercia</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Æthelbald was king of Mercia from 716 to 757 and the dominant ruler of southern England for much of his reign.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aethelberht-ii-of-east-anglia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelberht-ii-of-east-anglia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Æthelberht II of East Anglia</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Æthelberht II was king of East Anglia in the late 8th century, known from a few coins and later accounts.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aethelberht-of-kent"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelberht-of-kent.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Æthelberht of Kent</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Æthelberht was king of Kent from about 589 to 616 and the first English king to accept Christianity.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aethelflaed"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelflaed.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Æthelflæd</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Æthelflæd, Lady of the Mercians, was the eldest daughter of Alfred the Great and ruled English Mercia from the death of her husband Æthelred in 911 until her own death…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aethelfrith-of-northumbria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelfrith-of-northumbria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Æthelfrith of Northumbria</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Æthelfrith was king of Bernicia from about 593 and, from about 604, also of Deira, uniting them as the first ruler of Northumbria.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aethelred-i-of-wessex"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelred-i-of-wessex.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Æthelred I of Wessex</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Æthelred I was king of Wessex from 865 to 871, the fourth son of Æthelwulf to reign.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aethelred-of-mercia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelred-of-mercia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Æthelred of Mercia</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Æthelred was king of Mercia from 675 to 704, a son of Penda.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aethelred-the-unready"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelred-the-unready.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Æthelred the Unready</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Æthelred the Unready was king of the English from 978 to 1016, apart from a brief exile in 1013–1014; his nickname means 'poorly advised'.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aethelred-lord-of-the-mercians"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelred-lord-of-the-mercians.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Æthelred, Lord of the Mercians</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Æthelred was the ruler of English Mercia from about 881 until his death in 911, after the Danes had taken the eastern half of the kingdom.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aethelstan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelstan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Æthelstan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Æthelstan was king of the Anglo-Saxons from 924 and the first king of all England from 927, when he took York and received the submission of northern rulers.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aethelswith"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelswith.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Æthelswith</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Æthelswith was the daughter of King Æthelwulf of Wessex and sister of Alfred the Great.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aethelthryth"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelthryth.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Æthelthryth</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Æthelthryth, also known as Etheldreda or Audrey, was an East Anglian princess, a daughter of King Anna.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/oethelwald-of-deira"><span class="enc-name">Œthelwald of Deira</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Œthelwald of Deira was king of Deira from about 651 to 655, a son of Oswald of Northumbria, appointed under his uncle Oswiu.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aethelwealh-of-sussex"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelwealh-of-sussex.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Æthelwealh of Sussex</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Æthelwealh was king of the South Saxons in the later 7th century and the first Christian king of Sussex.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aethelwold-aetheling"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelwold-aetheling.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Æthelwold ætheling</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Æthelwold was a West Saxon prince, the son of King Æthelred I and cousin of Edward the Elder.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aethelwulf-of-wessex"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelwulf-of-wessex.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Æthelwulf of Wessex</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Æthelwulf was king of Wessex from 839 to 858, the son of Ecgberht.</span></a></li></ul>
